From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] LQ/SQ: alinhar o endereco em 16 bytes

O que quebrou:
  LQ e SQ liam/escreviam 16 bytes a partir do endereco exato (rs + imm).

Por que:
  No R5900, LQ/SQ ignoram os 4 bits baixos do endereco em silencio, sem
  excecao de alinhamento (EE Core Instruction Set Manual; PCSX2
  R5900OpcodeImpl.cpp LQ/SQ: "addr & ~0xf", com comentario explicando).
  O tradutor passava o endereco cru para READ128/WRITE128, que nao alinham.

A correcao:
  O endereco gerado vira (rs + imm) & ~0xF.
  LQC2/SQC2 NAO foram mudados: o PCSX2 nao alinha esses dois e nao ha
  evidencia sobre o hardware (docs/findings/14 s.5, em aberto).

Como foi achado:
  Testes LqIgnoresLowFourBits / SqIgnoresLowFourBits
  (tests/instructions/test_ee_instructions.cpp), docs/findings/14 s.5.

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp
index 7684097..639c416 100644
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/instruction_translator.cpp
@@ -196,9 +196,11 @@ namespace ps2recomp
         case OPCODE_SW:
             return genWrite(32, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate), fmt::format("GPR_U32(ctx, {})", inst.rt)) + ";";
         case OPCODE_LQ:
-            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, {});", inst.rt, genRead(128, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate)));
+            // LQ/SQ ignore the low 4 address bits instead of raising an address error
+            // (EE Core manual; PCSX2 R5900OpcodeImpl.cpp LQ/SQ: addr & ~0xf).
+            return fmt::format("SET_GPR_VEC(ctx, {}, {});", inst.rt, genRead(128, fmt::format("(ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {}) & ~0xFu)", inst.rs, inst.simmediate)));
         case OPCODE_SQ:
-            return genWrite(128, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate), fmt::format("GPR_VEC(ctx, {})", inst.rt)) + ";";
+            return genWrite(128, fmt::format("(ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {}) & ~0xFu)", inst.rs, inst.simmediate), fmt::format("GPR_VEC(ctx, {})", inst.rt)) + ";";
         case OPCODE_LD:
             return fmt::format("SET_GPR_U64(ctx, {}, {});", inst.rt, genRead(64, fmt::format("ADD32(GPR_U32(ctx, {}), {})", inst.rs, inst.simmediate)));
         case OPCODE_SD:
